WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.518 --> 00:00:04.543
Five boxes, one founder, and one tool in each box.

2
00:00:04.563 --> 00:00:07.854
Here's how to match each role to the right kind of help.

3
00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:16.684
Your chief of staff watches email and calendar and messages you first, so it's an always-on agent, like Claude Duet or a dot.

4
00:00:16.763 --> 00:00:27.234
Sales and customers runs on a schedule: an always-on agent with drafts, or a Grok Bot working in your CRM, with sending behind approval.

5
00:00:27.287 --> 00:00:33.083
Marketing and content benefits from you in the loop, so use a chat or desktop agent.

6
00:00:33.103 --> 00:00:38.714
The finance assistant organizes and drafts, like Claude Cowork on a receipts folder.

7
00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:40.692
Paying stays yours.

8
00:00:40.712 --> 00:00:45.737
Product and website goes to Cursor or Codex, with the code on GitHub.

9
00:00:45.757 --> 00:00:49.703
The rule across all five: one agent, one owner.

10
00:00:49.723 --> 00:00:54.523
Two agents on one inbox means conflicting drafts and wasted usage.

11
00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:56.261
Next: the role card.

